      "id": "PROOF_GAP",
      "title": "Unverified claims dominate coverage",
      "observation": "Ten of 24 extracted claims circulate in secondary or aggregator coverage without a primary source behind them.",
      "cost": "An investor reviewing the profile will notice many unverified statements, which can erode trust and increase due‑diligence friction. The lack of primary sources may cause the investor to request additional proof before committing.",
      "fix": "Publish the original sources for each claim on a dedicated page and update the coverage to link to them."
    },
    {
      "id": "CADENCE_GAP",
      "title": "Long silence between updates",
      "observation": "Across 8 datable public artifacts the longest silence was 26 months, between 2021-05-28 and 2023-08-05.",
      "cost": "A journalist will see a multi‑year gap and may question the founder’s ongoing relevance, potentially lowering interest. The silence can be interpreted as a lack of activity or transparency.",
      "fix": "Release a brief update or commentary dated today that references recent activities and link it to the existing artifact list."
    },
    {
      "id": "NARRATIVE_OWNERSHIP_GAP",
      "title": "Third‑party narrative dominates",
      "observation": "16 of 19 public sources are written by third parties, against 3 the subject controls.",
      "cost": "A prospective LP will find that most information comes from outsiders, making it harder to gauge the founder’s voice and strategy. This may lead the LP to seek additional direct communication before proceeding.",
      "fix": "Write and publish a new article or blog post under the founder’s byline that addresses key messages and distribute it through owned channels."
    }
  ]
